   \[
   3 \text{ ft} \times 30.48 \text{ cm/ft} = 91.44 \text{ cm}  
   6 \text{ in} \times 2.54 \text{ cm/in} = 15.24 \text{ cm}  
   \text{Total height} = 91.44 + 15.24 = 106.68 \text{ cm}
   \]

3. **Calculate BSA using the Mosteller formula:**  
   \[
   \text{BSA} = \sqrt{\frac{106.68 \times 29.48}{3600}} = \sqrt{\frac{3144.99}{3600}} = \sqrt{0.8736} = 0.935 \text{ m}^2
   \]

4. **Calculate the daily dose:**  
   \[
   0.935 \text{ m}^2 \times 17.5 \text{ mg/m}^2/\text{day} = 16.36 \text{ mg/day}
   \]

   The patient should receive **$\boxed{16.36 \text{ mg}}$** of the drug daily.
